@startuml class-diagram
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

title Class Diagram — BiblioTech (Clean 4 Layers, v0.5.1)

' ===================== Entities (Clean core, cero imports framework) =====================
package "Entities (Enterprise Business Rules — Dependency Rule: nada externo)" {
  enum Role {
    Admin
    Professor
    Student
  }

  class User {
    + id: number
    + email: string
    + passwordHash: string
    + role: Role
    + tokenVersion: number
    + create(data): User
    + toPublic(): {id,email,role}
  }

  class Material {
    + id: number
    + title: string
    + author: string
    + subject: string <<optional>>
    + year: number <<optional>>
    + edition: string <<optional>>
    + tags: string[] <<optional>>
    + ownerId: number
    + blobId: number
    + createdAt: datetime
    + create(data): Material
    + isOwnedBy(userId): boolean
    + applyPatch(patch): void
    + toPublic(): MaterialDTO
  }

  class FileBlob {
    + id: number
    + storageKey: string
    + fileName: string <<normalizado, NFR-005>>
    + mime: string
    + sizeBytes: number
    + contentHash: string <<informativo, no-unico>>
    + createdAt: datetime
    + create(data): FileBlob
  }

  class AuthSession <<Value Object, transitorio — NO persistido>> {
    + token: string
    + userId: number
    + role: Role
    + expiresAt: datetime
    + isExpired(now): boolean
    + toPublic(): {userId,role}
  }
}

' ===================== Use Cases (Application Business Rules = Controller de eventos) =====================
package "Use Cases (Application Rules — un punto de entrada por evento de sistema)" {
  class RegisterUserUseCase {
    + execute(input): AuthResult
  }
  class LoginUseCase {
    + execute(input): AuthResult
  }
  class UploadMaterialUseCase {
    + execute(input): MaterialDTO
    - assertCanUpload(callerRole): void
  }
  class SearchCatalogUseCase {
    + execute(query): Page<Material>
    + getById(id): Material
  }
  class ManageMaterialUseCase {
    + deleteMaterial(input): void
    + updateMaterial(input): MaterialDTO
    - assertAdmin(callerRole): void
  }
  class ManageUsersUseCase {
    + deleteUser(input): void
    + listUsers(callerRole): UserDTO[]
    + changeUserRole(input): UserDTO
    - assertAdmin(callerRole): void
  }
  class DownloadFileUseCase {
    + execute(input): FileDownload
  }
}

' ===================== Ports (owned by Use Cases; Dependency Inversion) =====================
package "Ports (interfaces en la capa Use Cases — Indirection/DIP)" {
  interface UserRepository {
    + findByEmail(email): User
    + findById(id): User
    + findAll(): User[]
    + save(user): User
    + listOwnedStorageKeys(userId): string[]
    + deleteCascade(userId): void
  }
  interface MaterialRepository {
    + save(material): Material
    + findById(id): Material
    + search(filters,page,limit): Page<Material>
    + deleteWithBlob(id): void
  }
  interface FileBlobRepository {
    + save(blob): FileBlob
    + findById(id): FileBlob
    + delete(id): void
  }
  interface FileStorage {
    + store(buffer,originalName): storageKey
    + stream(key): Stream
    + remove(key): void
  }
  interface PasswordHasher {
    + hash(plain): string
    + compare(plain,hash): boolean
  }
  interface TokenSigner {
    + sign(payload): string
    + verify(token): TokenPayload
  }
  class TokenPayload <<value object>> {
    + userId: number
    + role: Role
    + ver: number
  }
  interface ValidatorPort {
    + validateEmail(email): void
    + validatePassword(password): void
    + validateMetadata(meta): void
    + validateFile(mime,sizeBytes): void
    + normalizeFileName(name): string
  }
}

' ===================== Interface Adapters =====================
package "Interface Adapters (HTTP / DB / FS / validación -> puertos)" {
  class AuthController <<Controller-Adapter>>
  class MaterialsController <<Controller-Adapter>>
  class UsersController <<Controller-Adapter>>
  class JwtAuthGuard <<Adapter — 401 primero>>
  class RolesGuard <<Adapter — 403 por rol>>
  class DomainErrorMapper <<Adapter — DomainError -> HTTP>>
  class BiblioValidator <<implements ValidatorPort>>
  class TypeOrmUserRepository <<implements UserRepository>>
  class TypeOrmMaterialRepository <<implements MaterialRepository>>
  class TypeOrmFileBlobRepository <<implements FileBlobRepository>>
  class DiskFileStorage <<implements FileStorage>>
}

' ===================== Frameworks & Drivers =====================
package "Frameworks & Drivers (detalle reemplazable)" {
  class AppModule <<DI/Factory wiring>>
  class BcryptHasher <<implements PasswordHasher>>
  class JwtTokenSigner <<implements TokenSigner>>
  class NestJS <<framework>>
  class MariaDB <<database 11>>
  class LocalFS <<uploads/ folder>>
  class "React SPA" as SPA <<client>>
}

' ===================== Realizations (Adapter -> Port) =====================
BiblioValidator ..|> ValidatorPort
TypeOrmUserRepository ..|> UserRepository
TypeOrmMaterialRepository ..|> MaterialRepository
TypeOrmFileBlobRepository ..|> FileBlobRepository
DiskFileStorage ..|> FileStorage
BcryptHasher ..|> PasswordHasher
JwtTokenSigner ..|> TokenSigner

' ===================== Relations (UseCases -> Entities / Ports) =====================
RegisterUserUseCase ..> User : creates (Creator)
UploadMaterialUseCase ..> Material : creates (Creator)
UploadMaterialUseCase ..> FileBlob : creates (Creator)
ManageMaterialUseCase ..> Material : isOwnedBy / applyPatch (Info Expert)

RegisterUserUseCase ..> UserRepository
RegisterUserUseCase ..> PasswordHasher
RegisterUserUseCase ..> TokenSigner
RegisterUserUseCase ..> ValidatorPort
LoginUseCase ..> UserRepository
LoginUseCase ..> PasswordHasher
LoginUseCase ..> TokenSigner
LoginUseCase ..> ValidatorPort
LoginUseCase ..> AuthSession : construye (transitorio)
UploadMaterialUseCase ..> ValidatorPort
UploadMaterialUseCase ..> FileStorage
UploadMaterialUseCase ..> MaterialRepository
UploadMaterialUseCase ..> FileBlobRepository
SearchCatalogUseCase ..> MaterialRepository
ManageMaterialUseCase ..> MaterialRepository
ManageMaterialUseCase ..> FileStorage
ManageMaterialUseCase ..> ValidatorPort
ManageUsersUseCase ..> UserRepository
ManageUsersUseCase ..> MaterialRepository : deleteCascade (C-2)
ManageUsersUseCase ..> FileStorage
ManageUsersUseCase ..> TokenSigner : bump tokenVersion (NFR-006)
DownloadFileUseCase ..> MaterialRepository
DownloadFileUseCase ..> FileBlobRepository
DownloadFileUseCase ..> FileStorage

' ===================== Relations (Adapters -> UseCases) =====================
AuthController ..> RegisterUserUseCase
AuthController ..> LoginUseCase
MaterialsController ..> UploadMaterialUseCase
MaterialsController ..> SearchCatalogUseCase
MaterialsController ..> ManageMaterialUseCase
MaterialsController ..> DownloadFileUseCase
UsersController ..> RegisterUserUseCase
UsersController ..> ManageUsersUseCase
JwtAuthGuard ..> TokenSigner : verify -> TokenPayload{ver}
JwtAuthGuard ..> UserRepository : lee token_version (NFR-006, ADR-0004)
AppModule ..> MariaDB
AppModule ..> LocalFS
SPA ..> AuthController

' ===================== GRASP notes =====================
note right of Material
  Entity — FR-004/FR-012/FR-013 / UC-002/UC-004
  [Information Expert] isOwnedBy decide ownership
  local (C-1 -> 403). Reemplaza el feature-envy
  User.isOwner(materialId) (BT-05 §4).
end note
note right of AuthSession
  [Information Expert] solo conoce token/userId/
  role/exp y decide isExpired. Cero crypto: el
  hashing/firma vive tras PasswordHasher/TokenSigner
  (BT-06 §2). No persiste: JWT es stateless.
end note
note right of ManageMaterialUseCase
  [Controller + High Cohesion] material only:
  C-1/C-3 borrado + FR-013 edición. Split por
  agregado desde ManageMaterialUseCase único
  (BT-05 §4); Users en ManageUsersUseCase.
end note
note right of ManageUsersUseCase
  [Controller + High Cohesion] cuenta/rol only:
  C-2 cascada, listar, FR-011 cambio de rol
  (bump tokenVersion -> NFR-006).
end note
note right of ValidatorPort
  [Pure Fabrication + Protected Variations]
  helper sin encaje en dominio; cada regla es
  una Strategy (GoF) tras el puerto (ADR-0002).
  normalizeFileName cumple NFR-005 (BT-10).
end note
note bottom of AppModule
  [Creator/Factory] AppModule cablea puertos ->
  adapters por DI de Nest. MariaDB/LocalFS/SPA
  son detalle reemplazable.
end note
note bottom of UserRepository
  [Indirection] UseCases y adapters dependen de
  interfaces, no entre si. Dependency Rule:
  Frameworks -> Adapters -> UseCases -> Entities.
end note
@enduml
